Core Dossier Sections

Teaching Philosophy: Constructivist, evidence-based, and technology-integrated pedagogy emphasizing theory-to-practice bridging, transparent assessment rubrics, and inclusive classroom practice.

Instructional Experience: Higher education teaching and academic leadership across the University of Uyo and Goshen Wills College of Education, including seminar facilitation, test construction, item analysis, and student research supervision.

Evaluations & Referees: Student evaluation summaries, qualitative feedback, peer/administrative appraisal excerpts, and academic referee details.

Included Course Syllabi & Rubrics

EDU 611 (M.Ed.): Psychology of Attitudes and Human Values (12-week seminar outline, continuous assessment scheme, and empirical scale construction rubric).

EDU 223 (200 Level): Educational Technology (including instructional design models, digital/AI tools, and improvised teaching aid rubric).

EDU 211 (200 Level): Curriculum and Teaching Methods/Strategies and Psychology of Learning (12-week schedules, lesson note design rubric, and behavior modification assignment rubric).

PSY 121 (100 Level): Determinants of Behaviour (biopsychosocial and socio-cultural foundations with behavioral analysis term paper rubric).

EDU 311 (300 Level): Research Methods in Education (research design, sampling, validity/reliability, data analysis, and proposal rubric).

EDU 411 (400 Level): Psychological Testing (Classical Test Theory, item difficulty and discrimination analysis, norms, ethics, and item analysis rubric)
